{
 "schema": "polari-app/1",
 "id": "board",
 "package": "board",
 "title": "Board",
 "description": "Program real boards over USB / USB-C from Polari (brd arc): every register device as a BoardDefinition with its Road (track all, simulate few — the UNO first), USB adapters and programmer kinds as rows, cited datasheet facts, the two rules (USB from the host directly or via a known adapter; C / Verilog / SystemVerilog only) as selftests, and pol board detect over hwmap's scanner (brd-0, 2026-10-01); brd-1: the UNO end to end in plain C — gen around the AVR header, build (avr-gcc, sizes measured, refused past the cited limits), flash (DRY-RUN, a real run needs a detected board + --yes), the simavr twin at a pty, and the twin's measured object cost. brd-fi: the Firmware Installer App — firmware VARIANTS as rows (four different things to test on one UNO: the whole rig, blink-only, a raw ADC sweep as a second class UnoAnalogState, echo), compatibility judged on the generated header's sha256 + wire order against what this server generates now (never contract_hash alone), detect → builds that fit → DRY-RUN plan → confirm → install (on the host holding the port only) → the generated bridge attached → the rows arriving, on /display/firmware-installer. brd-wire (grpc-j4): the computer<->firmware mapping — hardware-interface bindings tie each row to one board interface, the wire v2 prelude carries the instance index (its width/representation a function of the bound count) + presence bits, enum mappings, contract hash v2 in compat, uno-pair (the same firmware for instance 0 and 1), and GET /api/board/instances/<id>/interface (the binding chain to the datasheet). sc-3 (D-sc-4 ruled: the ESP32-C3): an ESP-IDF C template (FreeRTOS tasks, the same SimRigState frames on UART0, FreeRTOS trace hooks on UART1), gen/build through the prf-esp-engines worker (ESP-IDF v5.5.5, reproducible images), flash as the exact esptool argv (DRY-RUN), and the twin in Espressif's QEMU fork (qemu:esp32c3) at a pty, its cost measured. brd-bo (PCB_FROM_SCRATCH_PLAN §2b, his ruling 2026-10-03): THE BOARD OBJECT — one board definition shared by KiCad, Zephyr, ESP-IDF/FreeRTOS, bare C and Polari, built around the pin/net assignment: BoardDefinition stays the Identity layer; SocDefinition + SocPin (the ATmega328P from its datasheet, the ESP32-C3 from Zephyr's dtsi + its datasheet), BoardHardware / BoardNet / Connector / ConnectorPin, BoardPin (pins named once), RuntimeProfile (per firmware_runtime, supported or refused), BoardView + BoardConflict; the UNO typed from Arduino's pinout (cited), the C3 INGESTED from Zephyr v4.4.2's esp32c3_devkitm board dir (stored, Apache-2.0); views generated out and ingested in by hash (pol board render|ingest|pins|conflicts|assign; GET /api/board/<board>/pins|views|conflicts); gen.py's pin constants and the C3 template's board_pins.h + sdkconfig board lines come from the rows, every image byte-identical.",
 "version": "0.6.0",
 "kind": "official",
